  "reusable": true,
  "title": "A SyncThread per-txn ACK can overtake the NEWLEADER ACK",
  "cause": "The update starts SyncRequestProcessor/SendAckRequestProcessor and hands off txns before the learner thread writes the NEWLEADER ACK; LearnerHandler treats the first ACK after NEWLEADER as the NEWLEADER ACK.",
  "trigger": "The learner thread is delayed longer than one append+fsync between logRequest and writing the NEWLEADER ACK.",
  "consequence": "Leader.waitForNewLeaderAck rejects the ACK as from a different epoch and the real NEWLEADER ACK is ignored; the leader does not form its NEWLEADER quorum and stalls until the init limit.",
  "sites": [
    "Learner.java:syncWithLeader NEWLEADER case",
    "LearnerHandler.java:run NEWLEADER ACK read",
    "Leader.java:waitForNewLeaderAck"
  ],
  "actions": [],
  "invariants": [],
  "premises": [
    "SyncThread can write a per-txn ACK before the learner thread writes the NEWLEADER ACK."
  ],
